<section class="institution-banner"><div><h1>About Us</h1><p>Learn about Alternate Energies, our purpose and our approach to solar energy for homes and businesses.</p></div></section>
<section class="company-profile">
  <div class="profile-copy"><h2>Our Profile</h2><p>Alternate Energies Limited is a private limited company incorporated in England and Wales on <strong>14 July 2011</strong>. Our registered business activity is the production of electricity.</p><p>We offer solar installation, maintenance, commercial rooftop partnerships and power supplied directly from our solar systems. We welcome enquiries from across East Africa, London and Norwich, with each project considered according to its location and requirements.</p><p>Our approach starts with understanding your property and energy needs, assessing the possibilities and agreeing a clear scope of work.</p>
  <div class="purpose-grid"><article><h3>Our Vision</h3><p>A future where solar energy makes a practical, lasting contribution to homes, businesses and the communities around them.</p></article><article><h3>Our Mission</h3><p>To help customers explore, adopt and care for solar systems through clear advice, considered planning and long-term relationships.</p></article></div></div>
  <figure class="profile-image"><img src="assets/solar-about.jpg" alt="Solar panels collecting sunlight under an open sky"><figcaption>Solar energy. A long-term perspective.</figcaption></figure>
</section>
<section class="company-values"><h2>Our Core Values</h2><div class="values-grid">
  <article><h3>Professionalism</h3><p>We aim to bring care, preparation and clear communication to every project conversation.</p><p>Understanding the site, agreeing responsibilities and explaining the next steps are central to our approach.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Transparency &amp; Accountability</h3><p>Customers should understand the scope of a proposal and the responsibilities that come with it.</p><p>We value straightforward discussions about suitability, costs, maintenance and what a solar system can realistically deliver.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Integrity</h3><p>Trust begins with honest information and realistic expectations.</p><p>We aim to recommend options that reflect the property and its energy needs, with terms discussed before work proceeds.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Customer Focus</h3><p>Every property and organisation has different priorities. We begin by listening.</p><p>Location, electricity use, timing and long-term plans help shape the options we explore with each customer.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Continuous Improvement</h3><p>We value learning from projects, customer feedback and developments in solar technology.</p><p>Our focus is on practical improvements that make information clearer and help customers care for their systems.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Working Together</h3><p>Successful projects depend on clear responsibilities and cooperation between customers, property owners and project teams.</p><p>We encourage open communication and a shared understanding of the work ahead.</p></article>
</div></section>
